CI install job of the CodeDev web app:

- run: npm ci --ignore-scripts
- run: npm rebuild bcrypt sharp     # the packages planInstallScripts allowed: reviewed name, version and integrity

package-lock.json in the PR under test:
"node_modules/progress-reporter-x": {
  "version": "0.2.0",
  "resolved": "https://registry.npmjs.org/progress-reporter-x/-/progress-reporter-x-0.2.0.tgz",
  "hasInstallScript": true
}

Statement: "In this job the postinstall script of progress-reporter-x does not run, while bcrypt and sharp still build their native code."

Allowlist (config/install-scripts.json), reviewed in August:
{ "name": "sharp", "version": "0.34.4", "integrity": "sha512-8b4c...e1f0", "reviewedBy": "reviewer-b" }

Dependency update PR in October, package-lock.json:
-  "node_modules/sharp": { "version": "0.34.4", "integrity": "sha512-8b4c...e1f0", "hasInstallScript": true }
+  "node_modules/sharp": { "version": "0.34.5", "integrity": "sha512-27d9...a3c5", "hasInstallScript": true }

Statement: "sharp is on the reviewed allowlist, so the install script of 0.34.5 can run without another review."
